import os,json,urllib.request,pathlib,base64
p=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent
prompt="""GPT-6.2-astra. Source reference is a Zeppelin-shaped lamp (realistic CGI, silver against black) with NINE OVERLAPPING AIRFOIL SCOOP SHELLS, not a stack of symmetrical elliptical flat discs. Current physically rendered CAD preview attached looks like ROUND ELLIPSES. Need correct actual CadQuery 2.8 solids.

VISUAL CLUE: In reference original, central horizontal shiny dark double rod at Z=111mm with small circular pivots. On LEFT half, every aluminum shell petal is anchored at a pivot x_i along rail and extends primarily TOWARDS CENTER to the RIGHT, forming a long lens/teardrop-like semicylindrical scoop. On RIGHT half each petal extends primarily LEFT toward center. The panel tapers to a point at its pivot and then rises into a smooth rounded upper scallop, with a short lower concave reflecting surface glowing warm. Outer shell near tips is tiny/pointed. Whole lamp silver upper hull dome, with symmetric smooth chain of scales, x span380mm, top z~167, bottom z~72, warm inside, chrome thin rail at z111, silver curved plinth. Each louver is SINGLE CURVED SHEET, NOT elliptical disc with a circle center hinge and not concave symmetrical half ellipse.

Current call make_louver(halfwidth,up,down,side,layer) makes symmetric ellipse spanning x±halfwidth, top z=up sqrt(1-(x/w)^2), bottom=-down sqrt, and a bent Y(X) surface with sag about10mm. We need ONE-SIDED RIGID SCOOP anchored x=0, extends in direction (+1 for left half, -1 for right half) to x up to length = 2*halfwidth. Upright shape: upper z rises from0 at x=0 to max up near x=50%-60% of length, returns0 near other tip; lower z dips by down; maybe x at other tip z0 creates smooth tear shape. Y curvature with bent sheet sin or circle arc across X, developable along Z, 0.6mm thickness, valid CadQuery solid. The center pivot x=0,z=0 should have little bracket tab/lug attached (can be separate). Use count e.g. 65 cross-section wires (quad loops, no degenerate near tips, ends at fraction .995), cq.Solid.makeLoft(...ruled=True), optionally cut pivot hole if material covers pivot; but if notch, don't force destructive holes. Keep actual STEP solids. Add orient parameter direction (1 or -1) to signature. Return ONLY compact executable Python code defining def make_scoop(halfwidth, up, down, side, layer, direction). Inputs other stdlib inside function. It will be used from an actual functional CAD assembly. No explanatory prose, no comments/docstrings, no image generation."""
body={"model":"gpt-6.2-astra","reasoning":{"effort":"high"},"max_output_tokens":5300,"input":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":prompt},{"type":"input_image","image_url":"data:image/png;base64,"+base64.b64encode((p/"renders"/"closed_front.png").read_bytes()).decode()}]}]}
req=urllib.request.Request("https://api.openai.com/v1/responses",data=json.dumps(body).encode(),headers={"Authorization":"Bearer "+os.environ["OPENAI_API_KEY"],"Content-Type":"application/json"},method="POST")
try:
 with urllib.request.urlopen(req,timeout=200) as r:response=json.load(r)
 result="\n".join(c.get("text","") for row in response.get("output",[]) for c in row.get("content",[]) if c.get("type")=="output_text")
 if result.lstrip().startswith(chr(96)*3):result=result.strip().split("\n",1)[1].rsplit(chr(96)*3,1)[0]
 (p/"astra_scoop.py").write_text(result,encoding="utf-8")
 print(json.dumps({"model":response.get("model"),"status":response.get("status"),"chars":len(result),"tokens":response.get("usage",{}).get("total_tokens"),"start":result[:180]},ensure_ascii=True),flush=True)
except Exception as e: print("ERROR",type(e).__name__,str(e)[:400],flush=True)
